<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n281" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbyssus</span></b> , i,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄβυσσος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίμνη</span>). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A bottomless pit</i>, <i>an
			abyss</i>, <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 13,
			20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>The sea</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen. 1,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>The place of the dead</i>, <i>Orcus</i>, <i>Hades</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Rom.
				10, 7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>Tartarus</i>, <i>hell</i>, where the
			wicked are confined, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Luc. 8, 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Apoc. 9,
			1</span></i>. So in eccl. Lat.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>